.claude/plans/PLAN-177/repass-rc4-20260816-t3-NOGO/transcript-rc4-2.log:9484: trailing whitespace.
+.claude/plans/PLAN-177/repass-rc4-20260813-NOGO/verdict-rc4-2.txt:3:   **Failure scenario:** If an adopter already has `.claude/.gitignore` without `/state/` and `/settings.local.json`, the helper returns without adding them. Under `--ceremony user`, the root `.gitignore` is deliberately untouched, so `/night-mode on` still leaves both artifacts visible to Git—the exact P1-1 defect. All efficacy scenarios start with no `.claude/.gitignore`, so their positive controls cannot catch this.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-177/repass-rc4-20260816-t3-NOGO/transcript-rc4-2.log:9486: trailing whitespace.
+.claude/plans/PLAN-177/repass-rc4-20260813-NOGO/verdict-rc4-2.txt:21:5. **P1 — The S303 harness filter creates a false-green class.**  
.claude/plans/PLAN-177/repass-rc4-20260816-t3-NOGO/transcript-rc4-2.log:9487: trailing whitespace.
+.claude/plans/PLAN-177/repass-rc4-20260813-NOGO/verdict-rc4-2.txt:23:   **Failure scenario:** The predicate never checks the known probe description/hash. Any markerless real spawn—including one admitted because the PreToolUse hook failed open—is classified as a harness probe and removed from the denominator. A direct probe using an unrelated description and hash returned green with `harness_probes_skipped=1`. The negative control adds one governed marker, so it never tests the dangerous all-absent/non-probe shape.  
